Hi Maria,

Here is a short note on the Q3 sales figures (July to September). The full report follows after the quarter close on 7 October.

- Coolers on rent at the end of September: 3,180, up from 3,050 at the end of June.
- UK: 1,720 coolers. Most growth came from plumbed-in coolers in London offices.
- Netherlands: 840 coolers.
- Germany: 620 coolers.
- Extra bottle orders were higher in July and August, as expected in warm weather.
- Paper cup sales were flat.

Eleven new clients signed in the quarter, mostly small offices. Unpaid invoices older than 60 days are below 2% of the total, which is the same as last quarter.

Kind regards,
Jonas
